-- Q25 [Evolutionary Patterns] hard skill2 ans=D
WITH q AS (
  INSERT INTO questions (section, topic, subtopic, question_text, options, correct_answer, explanation, difficulty, foundation, content_category, discipline, cognitive_skill, estimated_time_seconds)
  VALUES ('bio_biochem', 'Genetics and Evolution', 'Evolutionary Patterns', 'In the deserts of the Americas, the cactus lineage evolved thick, water-storing succulent stems, while in the deserts of Africa, the entirely separate euphorb lineage independently evolved strikingly similar succulent stems. The two lineages do NOT share a recent common ancestor. This pattern most likely reflects:', '[{"label": "A", "text": "divergent evolution from a shared ancestor"}, {"label": "B", "text": "adaptive radiation from one founder species"}, {"label": "C", "text": "homologous structures inherited from a common ancestor"}, {"label": "D", "text": "convergent evolution under similar selective pressures"}]'::jsonb, 'D', 'This is a Biology question that falls under the content category ''Transmission of Heritable Information from Generation to Generation.'' The answer is D because the scenario describes two lineages that do NOT share a recent common ancestor independently evolving the same succulent, water-storing form, which is the textbook definition of convergent evolution. OpenStax states that when ''similar phenotypes evolve independently in distantly related species... We call this phenomenon convergent evolution, where similar traits evolve independently in species that do not share a recent common ancestry.'' The shared succulent stem is therefore an analogous structure produced by similar selective pressures (arid environments), not by shared ancestry. The glossary likewise defines convergent evolution as the ''process by which groups of organisms independently evolve to similar forms.'' (Choice A) is incorrect because divergent evolution is the reverse situation, where ''groups of organisms evolve in diverse directions from a common point''; here the lineages started apart and became similar, not started together and became different. (Choice B) is incorrect because adaptive radiation produces ''multiple speciation events originating from a single species,'' radiating outward from one founder species, whereas the cacti and euphorbs descend from separate lineages, not a single shared origin. (Choice C) is incorrect because homologous structures are ''parallel structures in diverse organisms that have a common ancestor''; since these lineages lack a recent common ancestor, their similar stems are analogous, not homologous. (Choice D) is correct: similar succulent forms arose independently in unrelated desert lineages because comparable arid selective pressures favored water storage, the defining feature of convergent evolution. This is a Scientific Reasoning and Problem Solving question because you must apply the definition of convergent evolution to a described scenario and distinguish it from divergent evolution, adaptive radiation, and homology.', 'hard', '1C', 'Transmission of Heritable Information from Generation to Generation', 'biology', 2, 150)
  RETURNING id
)
